# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# ─── Cross-origin isolation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The AI Observer extension's ONNX Runtime asks for 2 WASM threads on Tier B,
# but resolveThreadCount() returns 1 unless SharedArrayBuffer exists AND the
# document is cross-origin isolated. Without these two headers the browser
# refuses both, and the extension logs:
#
#   [Runtime] Tier B asked for 2 WASM threads but got 1 (COOP/COEP missing)
#
# Serving them makes `crossOriginIsolated` true, so SharedArrayBuffer is
# available and the thread request can actually be honoured.
#
# ⚠ TWO CONSEQUENCES, BOTH DELIBERATE — READ BEFORE CHANGING.
#
# 1. `require-corp` blocks EVERY cross-origin subresource that does not send
#    `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy`. The only such resource this app loads is a
#    Supabase Storage signed-URL image in the evidence panels, and Supabase does
#    not send CORP. Those panels therefore prefer the inline base64 snapshot
#    (a data: URL, which COEP exempts) and fall back to the signed URL only when
#    no inline copy exists — see EvidencePanel.jsx. Fonts are bundled locally
#    via @fontsource and index.html loads nothing cross-origin, so nothing else
#    is affected. If a future feature adds a cross-origin image, script or
#    iframe, it will be BLOCKED here and the fix is CORP on that resource — or
#    switching to `credentialless`, which grants isolation without requiring
#    CORP, at the cost of sending those requests without credentials.
#
# 2. Cross-origin isolation is what lets ORT request a second WASM thread, and
#    CLAUDE.md records that forcing 2 threads previously broke ORT loading
#    outright (it spawns a proxy worker whose .mjs dynamic import fails inside
#    the content-script world). The guest demo does not use ORT at all — it runs
#    the bundled MediaPipe landmarker — so it cannot hit that. A real proctored
#    exam served from this origin could. Watch for a failed ORT session here
#    before assuming these headers are free.
# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
